    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0181" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/83: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-18T17:00:00+08:00">June 18, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 18—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>676. I have just received the following message from Mr. Maze, Inspector General
                    of Customs at Shanghai.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“In connection with the question of the integrity of the Manchurian
                        customhouses I write to inform you that I have received the following
                        telegram from the Dairen Commissioner for Customs which is
                        self-explanatory.</p>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>‘Received another despatch from Ministry of Finance dated 12th June
                            ordering me to remit Dairen customs revenue to Tung San Sheng
                                Kuan-yinhao<anchor n="55" xml:id="d96-f1"/> instead of to Shanghai,
                            saying that Changchun government will consider my disobedience as
                            expression of my hostile intentions and will take such measures as they
                            deem suitable and effective.’”</p>
                    </quote>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
